--
-- Test Description
-- This test verifies the operation of Wake-on-LAN using multicast hash
-- filter matches
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- * Checks that WoL is asserted for multicast hash matches.
-- * Checks that WoL is not asserted for unicast hash matches.
-- * Checks the operation of the WoL enable mask.
-- * Checks the operation of the "wol" output.
-- * Checks that the WoL is asserted for both good and bad frames.
--
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in 100M mode into a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--  3. Send the DUT various frames to test multicast hash detection for WoL:
--
-- Test 1: multicast hash match that generates WoL
--     Enable the multicast hash wake up event enable bit in the WoL register.
--     Send a good receive frame that matches the multicast hash.
--     Verify that the wol output is asserted for 64 clock cycles and that the
--     frame is successfully received.
--
-- Test 2: multicast hash match, but mask disabled
--     Disable the multicast hash wake up event enable bit in the WoL register.
--     Send a good receive frame that matches the multicast hash.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
-- Test 3: Not multicast hash matched
--     Enable the multicast hash wake up event enable bit in the WoL register.
--     Send a good receive frame that does not match the multicast hash,
--     but matches on unicast hash.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
-- Test 4: Bad CRC that generates WoL
--     Enable the multicast hash wake up event enable bit in the WoL register.
--     Send a receive frame with bad CRC that matches the multicast hash.
--     Verify that the wol output is asserted for 64 clock cycles and that the
--     frame dropped with a CRC error.
--
-- Test 5: Too short that generates WoL
--     Enable the multicast hash wake up event enable bit in the WoL register.
--     Send a short (60 bytes) receive frame matching the multicast hash.
--     Verify that the wol output is asserted for 64 clock cycles and that the
--     frame dropped with a undersize error.
--
-- Test 6: Good VLAN frame that generates WoL
--     Enable the multicast hash wake up event enable bit in the WoL register.
--     Send a good VLAN tagged receive frame matching the multicast hash.
--     Verify that the wol output is asserted for 64 clock cycles and that the
--     frame is successfully received.
--
-- Test 7: Multicast frame, but multicast hash is disabled
--     Enable the multicast hash wake up event enable bit in the WoL register.
--     Disable multicast hash matching.
--     Send a good receive frame that matches the multicast hash index.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted and that the frame is 
--     not recognised.
--     Receive a frame to trigger an interrupt and return the system back to
--     normal operating conditions.
--
-- Test 8: Broadcast multicast hash matched, no WoL
--     Enable the multicast hash wake up event enable bit in the WoL register.
--     Setup the hash index such that a broadcast frame will match and then
--     send a good broadcast receive frame.
--     Verify that the wol output is not asserted but that the frame is 
--     successfully received.
--
--  4. Check statistics for correct values from above tests.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--******************************************************************************
wait_states 3
bus_grant_delay 3


--******************************************************************************
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in 100M mode into a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--******************************************************************************
